### Typical Transformers Model Repository Structure

A typical Hugging Face Transformers model repository includes the following files:

| File                           | Purpose                                            |
| :----------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------- |
| `config.json`                  | Model architecture and configuration               |
| `model.safetensors`            | Learned model weights                              |
| `model.safetensors.index.json` | Weight-to-shard mapping for sharded checkpoints    |
| `tokenizer.json`               | Tokenizer vocabulary and processing data           |
| `tokenizer_config.json`        | Tokenizer settings and special-token configuration |
| `generation_config.json`       | Default generation parameters, if provided         |
| `README.md`                    | Model card, usage, and limitations                 |

> **Note:** A larger model may split its weights across several files, such as `model-00001-of-00004.safetensors`. The index file maps parameter names to their corresponding shards.
>
> A repository may omit some files or use alternative formats. Do not assume every model has exactly this structure.
